5789   F0FA             ;**********************************************************************************
5790   F0FA             ;* NMI Routines - This section of code is run only when the 
5791   F0FA             ;*                diagnostic switch on the CPU board is pressed.
5792   F0FA             ;*                It will test the hardware and report any errors
5793   F0FA             ;*                via the LED display on the CPU board. If all tests
5794   F0FA             ;*                are passed, the LED display will show '0' and
5795   F0FA             ;*                the code jumps to the normal power-up routines.
5796   F0FA             ;*
5797   F0FA             ;* Errors are as Follows:
5798   F0FA             ;*
5799   F0FA             ;*      0 - Test Passed
5800   F0FA             ;*      1 - IC13 RAM Fault (Most Significant Nybble)
5801   F0FA             ;*      2 - IC16 RAM Fault (Least Significant Nybble)
5802   F0FA             ;*      3 - IC17 ROM 2 Fault (Location $F000-$FFFF)
5803   F0FA             ;*      4 - IC14 ROM 1 Fault (Location $E000-$EFFF)
5804   F0FA             ;*      5 - IC20 ROM 0 Fault (Location $D000-$DFFF)
5805   F0FA             ;*      6 - Not Used
5806   F0FA             ;*      7 - Not Used
5807   F0FA             ;*      8 - IC19 CMOS RAM Fault or Memory Protect Failure
5808   F0FA             ;*      9 - Coin Door Closed or Memory Protect Failure or IC19 CMOS RAM Fault
